; UDON v2 Specification Bounded Context — Ubiquitous Language Schema in UDON
; Drawn from udon/spec/canonical.outline.md, spec/def/{AST,element,root}.md,
; spec/.kinds/term.kdl, and spec/.influx/at-defs/def-{binding,reference}.ud

|context[udon-spec] UDON v2 specification lexicon and AST value model.
  :uses [verisectorium]

  ; --- Lexicon Enums ---

  |enum[term-kind] Whether a term has its own file or is defined inline in the outline.
    |full-term    Defined in its own spec/def/<term>.md file with invariants and examples.
    |inline-term  Defined solely by its one-sentence row in canonical.outline.md.

  |enum[pos] Grammatical part of speech declared for guillemet form resolution.
    |noun
    |verb
    |adjective

  ; --- Value Objects ---

  |record[avoid-entry] A word deliberately avoided in favor of this term.
    :word   string
    :main   string

  |record[rel-entry] A directed semantic relation from one defined term to another.
    :verb     string
    :to       @term
    :card     card
    :note     string?

  |record[invariant-entry] A stated invariant whose failure breaks this term.
    :main   string

  |record[example-entry] A concrete example illustrating the term.
    :main   string

  ; --- Recursive UDON v2 AST Value Model (from spec/def/{AST,element,root}.md) ---

  |record[ast-attr] A named attribute on an element (unordered across distinct names).
    :name   string
    :value  string

  |variant[ast-node] A vertex in a parsed UDON AST (recursive, self-similar).
    |ast-element
      :name       string?
      :attrs      ast-attr*
      :children   ast-node*
    |ast-root
      :file       string
      :attrs      ast-attr*
      :children   ast-node*
    |ast-text
      :main       string

  ; --- Entity: Ubiquitous Language Term ---

  |entity[term] A spec-defined «term» in UDON v2's Ubiquitous Language.
    |trait-axis[mark]
      |draft      Suggested; not yet canonical or active.
      |accepted   Current decided and canonical for this spec version.
    |traits
      |foundation  Part 1 foundational term.
      |has-file    Backed by a standalone spec/def/<term>.md file.
    :kind       term-kind
    :pos        pos+
    :pl         string?
    :dual       @term?
    :synonyms   string*
    :backing    @verisectorium:piece?
    :main       string
    |children
      |avoid      avoid-entry
      |rel        rel-entry
      |invariant  invariant-entry
      |example    example-entry
      |prose      @term
